From 0f0860724a0cfc5e384ff372b5cb29ec5ccc42c1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ruscher <rruscher@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 15:52:54 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] server: Reloads the configuration on SIGHUP, or the
 ReloadConfiguration action.

Changing the configuration, the theme or the root menu required restarting
wlmaker, and with it the session. Configuration tools (eg. a converter of
Window Maker's preferences) had no way to apply their changes.

wlmaker_server_reload() re-reads the configuration file (the same that was
found on start, or --config_file) and applies:
 - KeyBindings: Replaced, if all of them bind; else the current ones stay.
 - Keyboard (XKB layout, repeat), Touchpad and Mouse: Applied to the devices.
 - WindowPlacement, FocusMode, Mouse.DoubleClickTime.
 - HotCorner.
 - The theme (--theme_file or 'ThemeFile'), as ThemeLoadFromFile does.
 - The root menu (--root_menu_file, or the default), unless it is open.
Anything failing to load keeps the current setting. Outputs, decoration
mode, screen lock, autostart and the state's workspaces still apply only on
start. The cursor's MoveWindowModifier applies to windows created
afterwards.

SIGHUP triggers the reload; the signal stays unblocked in launched
programs. The action 'ReloadConfiguration' (eg. for a key binding or a
menu item) runs it from an idle callback, since it replaces the key binding
or menu item that triggered it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
